      en: "Santa Fe Mega Farm, established in 2015 in East Berbice-Corentyne, is one of Guyana's largest agricultural enterprises, spanning 5,000 hectares. It specializes in soy, corn, and rice production, using irrigation from the Corentyne River. The farm operates a grain drying facility with a 500-ton daily capacity and employs 300 permanent and 500 seasonal workers. It also maintains a cattle herd of 2,000 head. Certified GlobalG.A.P. in 2020, the farm aims to reduce Guyana's reliance on imported animal feed. Despite economic benefits, it has faced criticism for deforestation and displacement of small farmers. Expansion plans include an additional 2,000 hectares by 2025.",
